  "id": "Compound::DB00674 - Gene::57053",
  "verbalization": "Galantamine is implicated in the regulation of acetylcholine-activated cation-selective channel activity through its interaction with specific proteins, which are part of a broader network of molecular mechanisms involving the channel activity of Chrna10. The evidence suggests that Galantamine binds to Chrng or Chrne, which in turn participate in the activation of cation-selective channels, ultimately leading to the participation of Chrna10 in this process. The varying scores across the paths indicate a consistent but not absolute relationship, suggesting that Galantamine may influence the functional activity of Chrna10 through a shared pathway involving acetylcholine-activated channels. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential role for Galantamine in modulating the expression or function of Chrna10, possibly through the regulation of ion channel activity. The mechanism is supported by the presence of multiple pathways converging on Chrna10, indicating a possible dependency on the activity of these channels.",
